At training, a prediction of Impatient Listener, at a position \emph{k},
is a Categorical distribution \emph{L}(\emph{m}:\emph{k}), con-structed
using a shared single linear layer followed by a softmax (with
\emph{m}:\emph{k} = (\emph{m}0\emph{, ..., mk})). Eventu-ally, we get a
sequence of \emph{t} + 1 distributions \emph{L}(\emph{m}) =
(\emph{L}(\emph{m}:0)\emph{, ..., L}(\emph{m}:\emph{t})), one for each
reading position of the message.

\begin{quote}
At test time, we only take the argmax of the distribu-tion generated by
Listener when it reads the EOS token.

